message.content:
{
  "summary": "This segment describes the functional architecture of neurons, detailing how they receive inputs via dendrites, integrate signals in the cell body, and transmit outputs through action potentials. It explains the mechanism of signal propagation along axons, including the role of myelin and nodes of Ranvier in enabling rapid saltatory conduction, while noting that intracellular electrical signals require synaptic mechanisms to influence other cells.",
  "topics": [
    "Neuron structure and function",
    "Signal reception and integration",
    "Action potential initiation and propagation",
    "Myelination and saltatory conduction"
  ]
}

