{
  "summary": "The segment defines synaptic plasticity as the activity-dependent capacity of synapses to alter effectiveness, distinguishing between long-term potentiation (LTP) and long-term depression (LTD). It details how NMDA receptors in the hippocampus link coincident activity to calcium signals that drive signaling pathways affecting receptor trafficking. The text emphasizes that plasticity mechanisms vary by synapse and stimulation pattern, noting that learning involves distributed network interactions",
  "topics": [
    "Definition of synaptic plasticity",
    "Long-term potentiation (LTP) and long-term depression (LTD)",
    "Role of NMDA receptors and calcium signaling in the hippocampus",
    "Variability of plasticity mechanisms based on stimulation patterns"
  ]
}

